-- title:
--   Constructing and retaining both block-source zeta tables
-- statement:
--   Let $h,J,c,p$ be natural numbers, $\delta$ an integer, and $q$ a global output. Put $W=512hJ$ and $K=\sum_{i\le c}\binom Wi$, with $c\le W$. Two arrays bijectively enumerate finite labeled inputs $X,Y$, preserving their integer values. Assume their exact residue histograms, the occurrence indices of $q$, and the local cover data are stored before the output region. Let $f,g$ be the corresponding left and shifted right block-source functions: admissibility-gated endpoint residue counts.
--
--   Assume the specified enumeration, preparation, and transform procedures, the ordered buffer layout, the retained-host space and word bounds, $S\le\Omega$, and $d+W+9\le\Delta$, where $S,\Omega,\Delta$ are the space, word magnitude, and depth limits. The call retains
--   $$\nu(b_L+jK+\rho(T))=Z_jf(T),\qquad
--   \nu(b_R+jK+\rho(T))=Z_jg(T)\quad(j\le W,\ |T|\le c).$$
--   Here $\rho$ is compact subset rank and $Z_j$ sums over deletions among the last $j$ coordinates. It meets the retained-host time budget and preserves every cell before the mask-output base.
--
--   This constructs reusable source transforms from the finite inputs and stored cover.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightBlockSourceRetainedHost.lean#L66-L217

